    "text": "I labelled all 8 columns of `pharmacy_claims_20261019.xlsx` and sent them to report_profile for job 1.\n\n- **rx_claim_id**: identifier, PHI (claim number tied to a person's prescription)\n- **member_id**: identifier, PHI\n- **fill_date**: date, PHI (a fill date tied to a patient's claim)\n- **ndc**: code, not PHI\n- **days_supply**: count, not PHI\n- **quantity**: count, not PHI\n- **paid_amount**: amount, not PHI\n- **pharmacy_npi**: identifier, not PHI (the pharmacy's provider ID, not a person's)\n\nThe file has no contract yet, so every column came back as \"unexpected.\" I marked the claim ID and fill date as PHI because they are tied to a patient's claim, so the contract writer should confirm that call.\n\nLabelled 8 of 8 columns.",
